From fa50092600c8b87323b583e905258d35c2cb5be3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:02:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): the jstack tree keeps to two type sizes and two
 weights, and a task's stage is three segments, crew, review and merge

Every name in the tree is 13px and every word beside it 11px, all at 400 but a root's name at
500. Levels step by ink and height: a root row 32px at full ink with 16px above it, a home 28px
at 85%, a worker 26px at 65%. A thread row under a project with no home is 13/400 and its status
11/400.

The seven stage ticks are three segments: the current one at full ink, amber when the task asks
you, the done ones at 45% and those ahead at 25%. The part of a review (review 1, fixing,
review 2) is only in the word. A scout draws none.
